From d97f09f5df83550d51793b506a069a3e5b024648 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hec <hec@heccraft.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 13:31:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] portals: add oo7 as secret portal

Mirroring this commit[1] on gnome-session. oo7 is being considered as
a replacement for gnome-keyring in Fedora 45,[2] and is already used in
GNOME OS.[3]

[1]: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-session/-/commit/3a77ebd28b07dac36efadc93df7ebb3dcb3155c9
[2]: https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Releases/45/ChangeSet#oo7_Secrets_Service_Provider
[3]: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-build-meta/-/merge_requests/4788

Signed-off-by: Hec <hec@heccraft.com>
(cherry picked from commit 02fdd8e7586110d6aa79d94f388756a3479091b6)
---
 docs/wiki/Important-Software.md | 2 +-
 docs/wiki/Packaging-niri.md     | 2 +-
 resources/niri-portals.conf     | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/wiki/Important-Software.md b/docs/wiki/Important-Software.md
index 56993e01..9262e3c2 100644
--- a/docs/wiki/Important-Software.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Important-Software.md
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ Portals **require** [running niri as a session](./Getting-Started.md), which mea
 
 * `xdg-desktop-portal-gtk`: implements most of the basic functionality, this is the "default fallback portal".
 * `xdg-desktop-portal-gnome`: required for screencasting support.
-* `gnome-keyring`: implements the Secret portal, required for certain apps to work.
+* `oo7-portal` or `gnome-keyring`: implements the Secret portal, required for certain apps to work.
 
 Then systemd should start them on-demand automatically. These particular portals are configured in `niri-portals.conf` which [must be installed](./Getting-Started.md#manual-installation) in the correct location.
 
diff --git a/docs/wiki/Packaging-niri.md b/docs/wiki/Packaging-niri.md
index 966638ab..3e5c33ba 100644
--- a/docs/wiki/Packaging-niri.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Packaging-niri.md
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ Set them as automatically-installed optional dependencies, if possible.
 - `xdg-desktop-portal-gnome`: required for screencasting.
 - `xdg-desktop-portal-gtk`: configured as the fallback portal in `niri-portals.conf`.
 (This is in general the standard fallback portal that you want installed.)
-- `gnome-keyring`: configured as the Secret portal provider in `niri-portals.conf`.
+- `oo7-portal` or `gnome-keyring`: configured as the Secret portal provider in `niri-portals.conf`.
 - Your distro's GPU driver package, such as `mesa-dri-drivers` and `mesa-libEGL`.
 Working hardware acceleration is required for running niri.
 - Some notification daemon like `mako`, generally required for apps to work correctly.
diff --git a/resources/niri-portals.conf b/resources/niri-portals.conf
index 3f13d669..377baff9 100644
--- a/resources/niri-portals.conf
+++ b/resources/niri-portals.conf
@@ -2,4 +2,4 @@
 default=gnome;gtk;
 org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Access=gtk;
 org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Notification=gtk;
-org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Secret=gnome-keyring;
+org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Secret=oo7-portal;gnome-keyring;
